Merged-main live proof passed on `f0b78f55d6d5acfb052a4512d97088b408a0c28d`, verified on `origin/main`. Exact PR head `e7cd48a0aecc6fb13a5820f0314fe9b62a73cbf0` passed [CI run 36262161690](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/36262161690) before auto-merge.

Provider: **blacksmith-testbox**. Lease: `tbx_01m3fgsbnbassrytjwk2nxs08w`; [run 36263879658](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/36263879658). In a clean detached checkout of that merged commit:

```sh
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm build
node /tmp/openclaw-ingress-crash-proof.mjs
```

Build passed in **368.81s**; live proof passed in **19.62s**. The controller starts each Gateway with `pnpm openclaw gateway run --port <isolated-port> --allow-unconfigured`, isolated home/state/config, and a synthetic plugin holding the normal `before_dispatch` hook. It sends an HMAC-signed Twilio-style POST to the actual Gateway SMS route. The provider credentials and event are synthetic; no external SMS service or operator Gateway is used.

Observed: an invalid signature returned 403 without admission; the valid request returned HTTP 200 with `x-openclaw-delivery-accepted: durable`. The claimed row was present before SIGKILL and remained durable after the actual Gateway PID exited. Restart replayed it into one controlled completion; duplicate deliveries, including across another restart, caused no additional dispatch. This demonstrates the selected crash window with at-least-once delivery and dedupe, not universal exactly-once external effects.

